": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 deploy (error rate 0.18). Release history: v2.2.9 and v2.3.0 healthy; v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 unhealthy. Action taken: rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The first rollback attempt halted partway with an orchestrator error after us-east had moved to v2.3.0, leaving the service mixed across regions; the retry completed and all three regions are now on v2.3.0. Post-rollback status: healthy, error rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure before re-deploying, and check the orchestrator partial-failure issue.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.3.0-2025"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so it may or may not have been created. I'll check the incident list before retrying to avoid a duplicate.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Lbp8GbwyY5RGLfH6ZBzrhk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It is healthy again with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was the failing release, and v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy. v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the service mixed across regions. I retried once with the same target, and that completed cleanly.\n- **Incident:** The create call timed out, so I checked the incident list before doing anything else. INC-0001 already existed with the full summary, so I did not open a duplicate.\n\nFollow-up: someone should investigate the v2.3.1 failure before it is re-deployed, and look into the orchestrator partial-failure issue.", "type": "text"}]}]}